Z||000000||DaveL||10-17-2001||08:00 AM||||I was able to remove one of the two tensioning rods on each of my headlight doors, and the action is much improved, quicker and more positive. They don't fly up at highway speeds either. Could there be any drawbacks to this?<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||LZeitgeist||10-17-2001||08:11 AM||||Hmmm... interesting. Never thought about that, but it *would* look cool to have 'quicker-action' headlights...<P>Like he said, anybody know of any drawbacks to this? <P>------------------<BR>Patrick W. Heinske  --  LZeitgeist@aol.com<BR>1988 Red Fiero Formula<BR>- 1st Place - Stock Coupe - FOCOSEVA 2000<BR>- 3rd Place - Stock Formula - FOCOA Nat'l 2001<BR>- Class Winner - 1982 to Present - 2001 Tarheel Tigers All-Pontiac Show||||reg||1
