Z||000004||Master_Sushi||10-18-2001||10:11 AM||||LOL off a cliff....<P>I had my old 88 coupe up pretty fast. I had the 85 speedo so im not sure what I was doing, but I had it wraped around to the 10-15mph mark. So I was hauling right along. RPMs were in the yellow also. I don't think the car would be to happy runing at those speeds for to long though. Oh, my headlights never came up either. Maybe I should have called my old coupe Herbie or something  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">.||||reg||12
Z||000005||revin||10-19-2001||07:46 AM||||I like the faster action lites. does it really keep them down at high speeds? I know that when I hit 90mph mine come up for air. Scared me crazy the first time. I thought the car was coming apart!! ha ha ||||reg||10
Z||000006||Formula88||10-19-2001||12:23 PM||||Well, it's going to make it more likely for the cover to come up at speed, but depending on the tension in your rod, it may or may not.  Not all Fieros have them come up anyway, so there's some tolerance there.  Perhaps the West Coast Fiero hold down cables in conjunction with removing one of the tensioner rods?<P>Also, if you have a vented hood, you probably won't notice this problem anyway.||||reg||1
